It has been observed that the inhabitants return to their destroyed houses, among their belongings that have drowned in the water and try to save anything they can find.
Hundreds of people have been injured, and hospitals have been damaged and destroyed by the 7.5-magnitude earthquake.
Some of the injured, including Dwi Haris, whose shoulder and back were fractured, rested outside the Palu Military Hospital, where patients were treated due to the continuation of strong aftershocks.
