Fishing and agriculture is the main economy in the center of Salavasi, especially in the coastal part of Dangala.
Nickel extraction is also important in the region, but most of the mines in Morovali are concentrated in the opposite part of Salavosi.
According to Indonesia’s Natural Disaster Management Agency, Palo and Dangala have been hit several tsunamis several times over the past 100 years.
In 1938, a tsunami killed more than 200 people and demolished hundreds of homes in Dangala.
Another tsunami in West Dangala in 1996 killed nine.
Indonesia is located in the Atlantic fire ring and earthquakes occur regularly.
A number of major earthquakes in recent years are as follows:
2004: A large earthquake on the west coast of Indonesia's Aque region in North Sumatra on December 26, which sparked a large tsunami and damaged 14 countries and killed 2,26,000 on the Indian Ocean coastline, more than half of which lived in Ake.
2005: A number of strong earthquakes shook the western coast of Sumatra in March and April.
Hundreds have been killed on Nias Island off Sumatra's coast.
2006: The 6.8-magnitude earthquake in southern Java, one of Indonesia's most populous islands, caused a tsunami that hit the southern coast and killed nearly 700 people.
2009: A 7.6-magnitude earthquake took place near the city of Padang, the capital of West Sumatray.
More than 1100 people were killed.
2010: A 7.5-magnitude earthquake on one of the Mantawai Islands occurred in Sumatra, causing a 10-meter-high tsunami that destroyed dozens of villages and killed almost $300.
2016: A shallow earthquake in the Pedi-Jaya area that took place in Ake and caused anxiety and fear in the people who remembered the deadly tsunami incident in 2004.
No tsunami occurred this time, but more than 100 people were killed by falling off the buildings.
2018: Large earthquakes took place on the tourist island of Lombek, which killed 500 people, most of the dead belonged to the northern part of the island.
The earthquake destroyed thousands of homes, and thousands of tourists remained temporarily unprotected.
